The hot path always passes both guards, so I marked that combined test `__builtin_expect(...,0)` to push the invalid case into a cold block and let the compiler lay out the single byte load as straight-line fall-through code.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect((profile == NULL) || (profileIndex >= profile->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```